# Programs of the shell that live in repositories of their own.
# build-rootfs.sh clones each at its tag, checks that the tag is still the
# commit given here, and runs its install.sh into the image. To build with
# a local checkout instead (one being worked on), set B8K_APPS_SRC to a
# folder holding it as <name>/. A program marked "private" lives in a
# private repository: without access to it the image is built without
# that program (b8k-apps leaves it off the panel), with a warning.
# A repository marked "apk" only releases Alpine packages (no install.sh):
# the image takes it from packages.lock and never builds it from source.
# "apk=a,b" locks only the packages named (the image needs no others).
#
# name     repository                                     tag    commit                                    [private]
